WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:30.000


2
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.541
<b>In this series of Chapter 5,</b>

3
00:00:32.541 --> 00:00:37.333
<b>Lord Krishna is mentioning the </b>
<b>importance of selfless Karma Yoga.</b>

4
00:00:37.333 --> 00:00:38.375
<b>But</b>

5
00:00:38.375 --> 00:00:41.958
<b>how to put Karma Yoga into practice?</b>

6
00:00:41.958 --> 00:00:47.000
<b>In this verse, Lord Krishna will explain</b>
<b>the three main characteristics of a person</b>

7
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.791
<b>who is established in selfless Karma Yoga.</b>

8
00:00:51.541 --> 00:00:55.875


9
00:00:55.875 --> 00:00:59.416
<b>When there is no attachment </b>
<b>left to the fruits of action;</b>

10
00:00:59.416 --> 00:01:04.666
<b>when actions are done with</b>
<b>full devotion as a duty –</b>

11
00:01:04.666 --> 00:01:08.250
<b>that is called selfless Karma Yoga.</b>

12
00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:13.208
<b>And the person who does this is </b>
<b>considered to be united with yoga.</b>

13
00:01:13.208 --> 00:01:16.416
<b>There are three characteristics </b>
<b>of a person united with yoga.</b>

14
00:01:16.416 --> 00:01:17.416
<b>First -</b>

15
00:01:17.416 --> 00:01:20.083
<b>one who is pure-souled,</b>

16
00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:23.000
<b>that is, whose intellect is pure;</b>

17
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:28.833
<b>that intellect which is not infected </b>
<b>by material desires and material delusions.</b>

18
00:01:28.833 --> 00:01:29.791
<b>Second -</b>

19
00:01:29.791 --> 00:01:32.166
<b>one who is self-controlled –</b>

20
00:01:32.166 --> 00:01:36.208
<b>that is, one who has gained </b>
<b>victory over their mind.</b>

21
00:01:36.208 --> 00:01:37.833
<b>The mind is fickle,</b>

22
00:01:37.833 --> 00:01:43.083
<b>which can never be stable due </b>
<b>to various desires and fears.</b>

23
00:01:43.083 --> 00:01:48.375
<b>But the mind of a self-controlled </b>
<b>person always remains in restraint.</b>

24
00:01:48.375 --> 00:01:49.291
<b>Third -</b>

25
00:01:49.291 --> 00:01:51.041
<b>one who has conquered the senses.</b>

26
00:01:51.041 --> 00:01:55.291
<b>One who has gained victory over their senses.</b>

27
00:01:55.291 --> 00:01:57.708
<b>Senses meaning sight,</b>

28
00:01:57.708 --> 00:01:58.583
<b>sound,</b>

29
00:01:58.583 --> 00:01:59.416
<b>taste,</b>

30
00:01:59.416 --> 00:02:00.291
<b>touch</b>

31
00:02:00.291 --> 00:02:01.666
<b>and smell.</b>

32
00:02:01.666 --> 00:02:05.708
<b>These senses always want to satisfy themselves.</b>

33
00:02:05.708 --> 00:02:11.750
<b>The Karma Yogi who gains victory </b>
<b>over them is called united with yoga.</b>

34
00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:14.125
<b>The one united with yoga, possessing </b>
<b>these three characteristics,</b>

35
00:02:14.125 --> 00:02:21.250
<b>performs their actions according to the </b>
<b>divine will without being bound by their actions</b>

36
00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:25.958
<b>and also becomes dear to </b>
<b>all beings while doing so.</b>

37
00:02:25.958 --> 00:02:29.500
<b>Now understand this in the context of Arjuna.</b>

38
00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:32.916
<b>Even if Arjuna engages in war,</b>

39
00:02:32.916 --> 00:02:36.583
<b>in which harm to others is inevitable.</b>

40
00:02:36.583 --> 00:02:37.583
<b>But,</b>

41
00:02:37.583 --> 00:02:43.083
<b>because, Arjuna is selflessly following </b>
<b>his duty, </b>

42
00:02:43.083 --> 00:02:47.125
<b>he is free from the bondage </b>
<b>of the fruits of his actions.</b>

43
00:02:47.125 --> 00:02:52.583
<b>When a person performs their actions </b>
<b>with a pure mind and devotion,</b>

44
00:02:52.583 --> 00:02:56.125
<b>then they become free from </b>
<b>the bondage of karma.</b>

45
00:02:56.125 --> 00:02:57.041
<b>But</b>

46
00:02:57.041 --> 00:03:04.458
<b>when a person externally renounces </b>
<b>their actions without purifying their mind,</b>

47
00:03:04.458 --> 00:03:10.541
<b>they live life struggling with </b>
<b>their own material desires.</b>

48
00:03:10.541 --> 00:03:14.791
<b>Lord Krishna is emphasizing that true liberation</b>

49
00:03:14.791 --> 00:03:17.458
<b>will not come merely from </b>
<b>the renunciation of actions.</b>

50
00:03:17.458 --> 00:03:23.666
<b>Rather, it is obtained by doing those </b>
<b>actions that are done selflessly</b>

51
00:03:23.666 --> 00:03:27.375
<b>and are dedicated to God.</b>

52
00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:32.166


53
00:03:32.166 --> 00:03:35.000
<b>While doing any work,</b>

54
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:40.625
<b>if your companion or </b>
<b>colleague makes a mistake,</b>

55
00:03:40.625 --> 00:03:45.083
<b>what is your first reaction,</b>

56
00:03:45.083 --> 00:03:49.375
<b>do you get irritated and say,</b>

57
00:03:49.375 --> 00:03:53.916
<b>'How can anyone make such a mistake?'.</b>

58
00:03:53.916 --> 00:03:55.833
<b>But</b>

59
00:03:55.833 --> 00:03:59.208
<b>if you thought with restraint at that time,</b>

60
00:03:59.208 --> 00:04:01.750
<b>you would realize</b>

61
00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:06.583
<b>that you have also made such mistakes.</b>

62
00:04:06.583 --> 00:04:10.208
<b>But can we do that?</b>

63
00:04:10.208 --> 00:04:12.125
<b>No, right!</b>

64
00:04:12.125 --> 00:04:14.791
<b>Think about it.</b>

65
00:04:14.791 --> 00:04:17.916
<b>The reason for such thinking is that</b>

66
00:04:17.916 --> 00:04:23.708
<b>there is no sympathy for others in your mind,</b>

67
00:04:23.708 --> 00:04:27.875
<b>there is selfishness for yourself.</b>

68
00:04:27.875 --> 00:04:33.166
<b>Evaluating the merits and demerits of others</b>

69
00:04:33.166 --> 00:04:40.375
<b>and working only for one's own </b>
<b>personal gain is called selfishness.</b>

70
00:04:40.375 --> 00:04:43.083
<b>Now the question arises,</b>

71
00:04:43.083 --> 00:04:47.041
<b>how will the mind become free from selfishness?</b>

72
00:04:47.041 --> 00:04:49.125
<b>This is possible when</b>

73
00:04:49.125 --> 00:05:00.250
<b>you gain spiritual knowledge and </b>
<b>understand that every person is a part of God.</b>

74
00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:06.708
<b>In such a situation, we can see</b>
<b>others with an equal vision, but</b>

75
00:05:06.708 --> 00:05:14.375
<b>to be able to do this, we have to imbibe</b>
<b>these three qualities in our lives.</b>

76
00:05:14.375 --> 00:05:16.375
<b>First of all,</b>

77
00:05:16.375 --> 00:05:20.333
<b>you have to purify your intellect,</b>

78
00:05:20.333 --> 00:05:24.416
<b>just as a pure-souled person does.</b>

79
00:05:24.416 --> 00:05:30.375
<b>With a pure intellect, a person can rise</b>
<b>above the vision of discrimination and</b>

80
00:05:30.375 --> 00:05:35.500
<b>see everyone with an equal spiritual vision.</b>

81
00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.583
<b>Secondly,</b>

82
00:05:37.583 --> 00:05:44.083
<b>like a self-controlled person, you have </b>
<b>to keep control over your thoughts.</b>

83
00:05:44.083 --> 00:05:47.625
<b>When thoughts are not in control,</b>

84
00:05:47.625 --> 00:05:54.958
<b>bad feelings like jealousy or </b>
<b>hatred give birth to selfishness.</b>

85
00:05:54.958 --> 00:05:56.666
<b>Third -</b>

86
00:05:56.666 --> 00:06:03.833
<b>like one who has conquered the senses, </b>
<b>you have to control your senses.</b>

87
00:06:03.833 --> 00:06:06.916
<b>When there is no control over the senses,</b>

88
00:06:06.916 --> 00:06:13.208
<b>many times in a rage you say something</b>

89
00:06:13.208 --> 00:06:20.583
<b>that causes immense pain and</b>
<b>suffering to the other person.</b>

90
00:06:20.583 --> 00:06:27.250
<b>Purity of intellect, control of thoughts </b>
<b>and mastery over senses</b>

91
00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:29.458
<b>are the three qualities</b>

92
00:06:29.458 --> 00:06:34.958
<b>that take you beyond selfishness and ego.</b>

93
00:06:35.666 --> 00:06:39.791


94
00:06:39.791 --> 00:06:47.875
<b>Having differences of opinion and</b>
<b>disputes in a family is quite natural,</b>

95
00:06:47.875 --> 00:06:51.583
<b>whether this dispute is </b>
<b>between husband and wife,</b>

96
00:06:51.583 --> 00:06:55.375
<b>or between children and parents.</b>

97
00:06:55.375 --> 00:06:57.666
<b>But</b>

98
00:06:57.666 --> 00:07:06.208
<b>when does a small difference </b>
<b>of opinion turn into a big dispute?</b>

99
00:07:06.208 --> 00:07:16.250
<b>This happens when the response to something </b>
<b>said in a rage is even more fierce and harsh.</b>

100
00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:22.166
<b>Arguments keep happening </b>
<b>between two people. But</b>

101
00:07:22.166 --> 00:07:27.208
<b>if even one of the two thinks to remain calm,</b>

102
00:07:27.208 --> 00:07:31.333
<b>is a dispute possible?</b>

103
00:07:31.333 --> 00:07:33.625
<b>not at all.</b>

104
00:07:33.625 --> 00:07:39.916
<b>To do this, first of all you</b>
<b>have to purify your mind.</b>

105
00:07:39.916 --> 00:07:46.708
<b>Like a pure soul, you have to empty</b>
<b>your heart of selfishness and ego.</b>

106
00:07:46.708 --> 00:07:48.500
<b>And when this happens,</b>

107
00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:51.875
<b>every member of the family will understand</b>

108
00:07:51.875 --> 00:07:56.250
<b>that everyone just wants the best for each other,</b>

109
00:07:56.250 --> 00:08:01.500
<b>and in such a situation, if someone </b>
<b>gets angry for some reason,</b>

110
00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:07.583
<b>the other can remain calm at that </b>
<b>time and end the matter.</b>

111
00:08:07.583 --> 00:08:13.833
<b>In this way, when every member of the</b>
<b>family imbibes these qualities in their life,</b>

112
00:08:13.833 --> 00:08:21.083
<b>even the most difficult times </b>
<b>cannot break that family apart.</b>

113
00:08:21.708 --> 00:08:26.000


114
00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:29.750
<b>In the business world of the modern era,</b>

115
00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:34.583
<b>everything is getting tougher day by day.</b>

116
00:08:34.583 --> 00:08:41.291
<b>Only those organizations and their </b>
<b>colleagues who easily adapt to this difficulty</b>

117
00:08:41.291 --> 00:08:44.833
<b>attain progress.</b>

118
00:08:44.833 --> 00:08:48.250
<b>But how?</b>

119
00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:51.750
<b>Through collective contribution.</b>

120
00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:57.833
<b>It is because of collective contribution </b>
<b>that various experts come together</b>

121
00:08:57.833 --> 00:09:00.875
<b>and make difficult tasks easy.</b>

122
00:09:00.875 --> 00:09:08.125
<b>If the top leadership of the organization</b>
<b>aspires contribution from colleagues,</b>

123
00:09:08.125 --> 00:09:12.166
<b>they have to promote these three qualities.</b>

124
00:09:12.166 --> 00:09:13.500
<b>First -</b>

125
00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:15.416
<b>pure-souled.</b>

126
00:09:15.416 --> 00:09:20.708
<b>That is, when all colleagues have internal purity,</b>

127
00:09:20.708 --> 00:09:27.708
<b>they will be able to align their goals with </b>
<b>the main objective of the organization.</b>

128
00:09:27.708 --> 00:09:35.416
<b>And in this way there will be no place</b>
<b>for personal selfishness or ego.</b>

129
00:09:35.416 --> 00:09:36.708
<b>Second -</b>

130
00:09:36.708 --> 00:09:42.333
<b>self-controlled. </b>
<b>That is, control over the mind.</b>

131
00:09:42.333 --> 00:09:45.041
<b>While solving a difficulty,</b>

132
00:09:45.041 --> 00:09:51.125
<b>there is always a possibility of negative </b>
<b>thoughts coming in any group.</b>

133
00:09:51.125 --> 00:09:54.333
<b>When frustration and disappointment </b>
<b>are at their peak,</b>

134
00:09:54.333 --> 00:09:59.666
<b>a small mistake by someone </b>
<b>can escalate the matter,</b>

135
00:09:59.666 --> 00:10:03.916
<b>a negative atmosphere </b>
<b>can be created. But</b>

136
00:10:03.916 --> 00:10:07.208
<b>if the quality of self-control is present,</b>

137
00:10:07.208 --> 00:10:10.708
<b>everyone's thoughts will remain in control.</b>

138
00:10:10.708 --> 00:10:12.625
<b>The third quality is -</b>

139
00:10:12.625 --> 00:10:14.416
<b>conquest of the senses –</b>

140
00:10:14.416 --> 00:10:20.166
<b>emotions are high during serious discussions,</b>

141
00:10:20.166 --> 00:10:24.958
<b>there is also a possibility of losing restraint.</b>

142
00:10:24.958 --> 00:10:31.166
<b>In such a situation, if all the colleagues </b>
<b>keep their senses under control,</b>

143
00:10:31.166 --> 00:10:35.916
<b>then they can think in a positive way.</b>

144
00:10:35.916 --> 00:10:40.958
<b>Pure-souled, self-controlled and one</b>
<b>who has conquered the senses –</b>

145
00:10:40.958 --> 00:10:43.375
<b>with the help of these three qualities,</b>

146
00:10:43.375 --> 00:10:50.833
<b>any organization and its members </b>
<b>can move towards progress.</b>

